  "body": "## SPEC\n\nReal evidence gathered 2026-08-15T10:51-10:58Z on VERIDIAN-DEV: the owner\ndispatch gateway had dispatched **zero** owner rows in 6.5+ hours. ~20 rows\nwith `task_kind=veridian_task_create` / `source_trigger=owner_dispatch_gateway`\nsat `status=queued`/`ts_dispatched=NULL`, submitted continuously from\n`2026-08-15T04:15:49` through `09:17:55`. Every one of the box's occupied\nconcurrency slots (`CONCURRENCY_CAP=5` at `dispatch_core.py:101`) held a\nresurrected `2026-07-18` task identity instead.\n\nUMR-20260815-105911-a2c9.\n\n## Root cause (real, proved with a live before/after query — see below)\n\n`dispatch_core.py` is only the concurrency-gating primitive (how many may\nrun) — it never decides *what* to dispatch. The real selection/ordering\nlogic is `resource_governor.py`'s `next_queued_task()` /\n`effective_priority()`, called from `dispatch_one()`.\n\n1. **`effective_priority(row, now)`** ranks every queued row by\n   `(tier - age-based promotions, ts_submitted)`. It ages *every* row at the\n   same rate, so a **same-tier batch arrival** can never be overtaken by a\n   later-arriving row at the same nominal tier — both age identically, and\n   the `ts_submitted` tiebreak always favors the older row. Aging alone can\n   never invert that relative order.\n2. **`dispatch-tick.py`'s `resume_interrupted_workers_tick()`** submits\n   *every* resumable `task.yaml` it finds in a single sweep, each stamped\n   with a hardcoded `tier=1` and a near-identical `ts_submitted`. Real,\n   live `superboss-register.sqlite` evidence: a single legitimate\n   credit-unblock sweep (`2026-08-15T03:56:09–04:15:xx Z`) — resuming 87\n   real `2026-07-18` `task_identity` rows that had been genuinely blocked\n   for weeks on a real, now-resolved OpenRouter negative-balance issue (see\n   `task-20260815-034138-resume-credit-blocked-backlog-after-real`) —\n   queued all 87 within ~20 seconds, all at `tier=1`. A second sweep\n   re-queued ~30 more at `08:42:46–08:43:00Z` the same morning (confirmed:\n   `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM umr_tasks WHERE ts_submitted BETWEEN\n   '2026-08-15T08:42:46' AND '2026-08-15T08:43:01'` → 30).\n\nCombined: a ~90-row same-tier batch permanently outranks any\n`owner_dispatch_gateway` row arriving after it, for as long as it takes the\nwhole batch to drain — a structural, indefinite-starvation defect,\nindependent of whether the `07-18` backlog itself was legitimate (it was —\nsee the resumed task's own checkpoint history, real credit balance\nre-verified at $19.85, well above the $0.10 floor).\n\n`directive_engine.py` / `recover-failed-workers.py` / `status-remediation-\ntick.py` were checked and are **not** involved in this path: `directive_\nengine.py` only drives `DIRECTIVE.yaml`'s own `priority_queue` (unrelated\n`task_identity` shapes, e.g. `PR617-REVIEW`), `recover-failed-workers.py` is\na standalone, manually-invoked 402-balance-only script, and\n`status-remediation-tick.py` only handles PR merge-retry mechanics. The one\nreal re-minting path for `task-20260718-*-retry-N-*` identities is\n`dispatch-tick.py`'s `resume_interrupted_workers_tick()`.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. **`resource_governor.py`**: `next_queued_task()` now applies a narrow,\n   additive starvation guard — once any `owner_dispatch_gateway` row has\n   been queued for `OWNER_STARVATION_GUARANTEE_SECONDS` (30min default,\n   `VERIDIAN_GOVERNOR_OWNER_STARVATION_GUARANTEE_S` override), the *oldest*\n   such row is picked next unconditionally, ahead of every other queued\n   row's tier/age. With no starved owner row, ranking is unchanged.\n2. **`dispatch-tick.py`**: `resume_interrupted_workers_tick()` now caps how\n   many real `resource_governor.submit()` calls it makes per tick\n   (`RESUME_SUBMIT_BATCH_LIMIT`, default 10,\n   `VERIDIAN_RESUME_SUBMIT_BATCH_LIMIT` override) — a large backlog now\n   trickles across multiple ticks instead of flooding the queue with dozens\n   of same-tier, same-timestamp rows in one shot. Real candidates past the\n   cap are left untouched (not marked dead/duplicate) for a later tick,\n   same as the existing concurrency-cap deferral already works.\n\nBoth fixes are additive and scoped: fix 1 is the hard guarantee (closes the\nstarvation regardless of what floods the queue); fix 2 reduces how badly a\nsingle sweep can flood it in the first place. Neither re-blocks the\nlegitimately-unblocked `07-18` backlog work.\n\n## Real before/after proof\n\nRan both the pre-fix (`git show 8fda6b8:resource_governor.py`) and the\npost-fix `next_queued_task()` against the **same real, live, currently-queued\nrows** in production `superboss-register.sqlite` (read-only connection, never\nmutated):\n\n```\n=== REAL LIVE queued rows (read-only), source_trigger breakdown ===\n{'owner_dispatch_gateway': 17, 'dispatch-tick:resume_interrupted_workers': 17}\ntotal queued: 34\n\n=== BEFORE (pre-fix resource_governor.py, real live queued rows) ===\n{'umr_id': 'UMR-20260815-040423-4658', 'task_identity':\n'task-20260718-130005-retry-2--ai-model-lifecycle---benchmark', 'tier': 1,\n'source_trigger': 'dispatch-tick:resume_interrupted_workers', 'ts_submitted':\n'2026-08-15T04:04:23.364503+00:00'}\n\n=== AFTER (post-fix resource_governor.py, SAME real live queued rows) ===\n{'umr_id': 'UMR-20260815-041549-27c9', 'task_identity':\n'owner-task-20260815-041548-3221254', 'tier': 1, 'source_trigger':\n'owner_dispatch_gateway', 'ts_submitted': '2026-08-15T04:15:49.722774+00:00'}\n\nreal live owner_dispatch_gateway rows currently past the 1800s starvation\nguarantee: 15\n  UMR-20260815-111843-28fc age=9346s  ...\n  UMR-20260815-105956-fdcd age=10473s ...\n  UMR-20260815-081903-82f3 age=20127s ...\n  ... (15 total)\n```\n\nThe fix changes the real dispatch pick from a `07-18` retry row to a real\nowner row aged 9.6+ hours past the guarantee — proving both that the defect\nis real and currently active, and that the fix closes it.\n\n## Tests (real, exit 0)\n\n- `tests/test_owner_dispatch_starvation_guard.py` — 3/3 pass. Proves (a) a\n  same-tier batch permanently outranks a later owner row *without* the\n  guard, (b) the guard picks the oldest starved owner row once its age\n  reaches the guarantee even against a larger/older batch, (c) with no\n  starved owner row the ranking is unchanged.\n- `tests/test_resume_interrupted_workers_batch_cap.py` — 2/2 pass. Proves\n  the batch cap bounds real `submit()` calls per tick and is a no-op when\n  the candidate count is already under the limit.\n- Full existing regression suite for both touched files re-run clean:\n  `test_resource_governor_queue_management.py` (13/13),\n  `tests/test_resume_interrupted_workers_bounded_retry.py` (2/2),\n  `tests/test_resume_interrupted_workers_no_duplicate_row.py` (2/2), plus a\n  16-file sweep of every other test importing `dispatch_one`/`resource_\n  governor`. 2 unrelated failures\n  (`test_run_tick_still_stops_on_row_independent_block`,\n  `test_dispatch_one_defense_in_depth_blocks_preexisting_queued_row`)\n  reproduce **identically** against the unmodified pre-fix baseline (real\n  live `running_worker_count()==5/5` on this box right now) — confirmed not\n  caused by this change.\n\nCites: SPEC evidence UMR-20260815-105911-a2c9; real live\n`superboss-register.sqlite` queries in this PR's own commit message and\ndescription above.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
